.TH 2048 1 "FUZIX Games" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
2048 \- slide the tiles and join them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 2048
.RB [ \-m ]
.RB [ \-s ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Frost-Phoenix's terminal version of Gabriele Cirulli's game, adapted for
FUZIX by Ciaran Anscomb.  Every move slides all the tiles on a 4 by 4
board as far as they will go; two equal tiles that meet join into one of
twice the value, and a new tile appears.  Make a 2048 to win.  The game
is over when nothing can move.
.PP
Colour is only drawn for a terminal type of
.B vt52
or
.BR xterm ;
on the console, whose type is
.BR pc3 ,
the board is plain.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-m
Monochrome, even on a terminal that has colour.
.TP
.B \-s
Small tiles, to fit a 32 by 16 screen.
.TP
.B \-h
Print a short help and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.RB "arrows, " w " " a " " s " " d ", or " k " " h " " j " " l
Slide up, left, down or right.
.TP
.B b
Take back the last move.
.TP
.B r
Start again.
.TP
.B Ctrl-L
Redraw the screen.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invaders (1)
